# ─── Testing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/coverage

# Test files stay local — they are not pushed with the app.
# `__tests__/` has no leading slash on purpose, so it also catches the suite nested
# under src/ (src/screens/DynamicDealCenter/__tests__/), not only the root folder.
# The loose patterns cover a test written beside the file it exercises.
__tests__/
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
*.spec.ts
*.spec.tsx
*.txt
tests
# ─── Markdown ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No markdown is pushed EXCEPT the Claude repo guide, so ticket write-ups and handoff
# notes stay on the machine that wrote them. What IS pushed:
#   CLAUDE.md        the root guide (and any nested CLAUDE.md)
#   docs/claude/**   its part files - CLAUDE.md §8 indexes them and doc-guard parses §8
#   .claude/**       Claude Code's own config (commands / agents / skills are .md files)
# CLAUDE.local.md is personal by design and stays ignored.
# NOTE: ignoring cannot untrack a file that is already committed; that takes `git rm --cached`.
*.md
!CLAUDE.md
!docs/claude/**/*.md
!.claude/**/*.md
# ─── Yarn Berry (not used, but safe to include) ───────────────────────────────
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/sdks
!.yarn/versions
yarn.lock
branch_structure.json
config.bat
# Generated at build time by the RN Gradle bundling task; never commit it —

# it bakes in .env values (API URL + keys) and goes stale.

android/app/src/main/assets/index.android.bundle
# Offline-module suites are tracked on purpose: the queues hold a rep's unsent work, so their
# rules must run in CI and on every machine. Everything else above stays local.
!tests/
!tests/**/*.test.ts

# MCP / Maestro tooling output - never commit (logs, debug dumps, UI-test artifacts, screenshots)
*mcp*.log
*mcp*.log.*
mcp-logs/
.mcp-logs/
.maestro/
maestro-*/
*.maestro-*
/*.png
!/app.png
